he n − p\nletter difference (probe check `f_equals_h_times_g`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BarParitySplitGap.no_F_with_ruledTrace_odd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BarParitySplitGap.no_F_with_ruledTrace_odd","kind":"theorem","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BarParitySplitGap.lean#L135-L149","doc":"Hence no `F : ℚ → ℚ` has (un-normalised) odd part `2•f` under `q ↦ q⁻¹`, whatever\nits even part. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BarParitySplitGap.ruledTrace_not_bar_odd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BarParitySplitGap.ruledTrace_not_bar_odd","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BarParitySplitGap.lean#L126-L133","doc":"The ruled trace is not bar-odd. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BarParitySplitGap.ruledTrace_witness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BarParitySplitGap.ruledTrace_witness","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BarParitySplitGap.lean#L123-L124","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BarParitySplitGap.barFun_invol","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BarParitySplitGap.barFun_invol","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BarParitySplitGap.lean#L120-L121","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BarParitySplitGap.barFun","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BarParitySplitGap.barFun","kind":"def","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BarParitySplitGap.lean#L114-L118","doc":"Bar on functions: `g ↦ (q ↦ g q⁻¹)`; linear and involutive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BarParitySplitGap.ruledTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BarParitySplitGap.ruledTrace","kind":"def","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BarParitySplitGap.lean#L107-L112","doc":"The ruled `Q_β` trace at `z_D` on `nuc11_interleaved`, as a rational function\n(probe `qbeta_bar_parity_split_gap_probe.py`, check `base_f_matches_recorded_closed_form`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BarParitySplitGap.zD_bar_shift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BarParitySplitGap.zD_bar_shift","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BarParitySplitGap.lean#L93-L105","doc":"Convention-D one-letter intertwining: `tr(σ⁻¹) = z − h` at `q` equals `tr(σ) = z`\nat `q⁻¹`, for `z = z_D = q³/(q²+1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BarParitySplitGap.odd_mul_of_anti","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BarParitySplitGap.odd_mul_of_anti","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BarParitySplitGap.lean#L88-L91","doc":"Odd part of a product with an anti element, for a ring involution. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BarParitySplitGap.trace_anti_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BarParitySplitGap.trace_anti_iff","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BarParitySplitGap.lean#L75-L84","doc":"Intertwining: `T (σA x) = σR (T x)` for all `x`. Then `T x` is σR-anti iff `T`\nannihilates the even part of `x`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BarParitySplitGap.exists_parts_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BarParitySplitGap.exists_parts_iff","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BarParitySplitGap.lean#L48-L73","doc":"With identity readouts, a common element exists iff the two readouts have the\nparities. The forward direction needs `V` to have no `2`-torsion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BarParitySplitGap.oddP","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BarParitySplitGap.oddP","kind":"def","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BarParitySplitGap.lean#L45-L46","doc":"Un-normalised odd part. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BarParitySplitGap.evenP","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BarParitySplitGap.evenP","kind":"def","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BarParitySplitGap.lean#L42-L43","doc":"Un-normalised even part. ","signatureChunk":0}]}